        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "But when king David heard of all these things, he was very wroth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 13:21",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "And Absalom spake unto his brother Amnon neither good nor bad: for Absalom hated Amnon, because he had forced his sister Tamar.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 13:22",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass after two full years, that Absalom had sheepshearers in Baal-hazor, which is beside Ephraim: and Absalom invited all the king’s sons.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 94,
            "end": 96
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 13:23",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "And Absalom came to the king, and said, Behold now, thy servant hath sheepshearers; let the king, I beseech thee, and his servants go with thy servant.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 13:24",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "And the king said to Absalom, Nay, my son, let us not all now go, lest we be chargeable unto thee. And he pressed him: howbeit he would not go, but blessed him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 13:25",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "Then said Absalom, If not, I pray thee, let my brother Amnon go with us. And the king said unto him, Why should he go with thee?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 13:26",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "But Absalom pressed him, that he let Amnon and all the king’s sons go with him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "2 Samuel 13:27",
        "book": "2 Samuel",
        "chapter": 13,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "Now Absalom had commanded his servants, saying, Mark ye now when Amnon’s heart is merry with wine, and when I say unto you, Smite Amnon; then kill him, fear not: have not I commanded you? be courageous, and be valiant.",
